#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# hold_pattern

#% text
# `hold_pattern(p)` is the pattern `p`, kept unevaluated where it is written.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Its argument is held: `hold_pattern(_ + _)` stays a sum of two blanks, where `_ + _` alone is evaluated to `2*_`.

#% item
# A rule kept in `hold_pattern` is a pattern for rules, not a replacement: `cases(xs, hold_pattern(_ -> automatic))` selects the rules with the right side `automatic`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
cases([1, b -> automatic, c -> 3], hold_pattern(_ -> automatic))
#% output
#= [b -> automatic]

#% cell
match_q(a + b, hold_pattern(_ + _))
#% output
#= true

#% cell
match_q(a + b, _ + _)
#% output
#= false

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `verbatim`, `quote`, `cases`
